# Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS and replace @owner with the people who review
# agent configuration. GitHub then asks them to review any pull request that
# touches these files. Required review needs branch protection; without it
# (GitHub Free with a private repository), this still requests the review,
# and the CI step "Agent configuration changes" flags the pull request.
#
# On a one-person project, where the agent opens pull requests as you, GitHub
# counts the owner as satisfied without a review, so this enforces nothing:
# the CI flag and your reading of the flagged files carry rule 18 instead.
#
# Agent configuration is code (rule 18 in the ai-playbook): hooks run on
# every session, settings change what the agent may do without asking, MCP
# servers reach other systems, and CLAUDE.md and the rules are instructions.

/.claude/                @owner
/.mcp.json               @owner
CLAUDE.md                @owner
AGENTS.md                @owner
/.github/workflows/      @owner
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @owner
/.devcontainer/          @owner
